{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cesgjcm7YQp1HfAYjEnac","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now I have a good understanding of the codebase. Let me announce and work through the analysis phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:ANALYSIS>>\n```\n\n**Requirement, restated in one sentence:**\nAdd a POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint that cancels active orders, persists the status change, cancels their CREATED shipments, rejects repeated attempts only if a CONFIRMED shipment exists, and forbids creating new shipments for cancelled orders.\n\n**Repository findings:**\n- Order entity lacks status: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/Order.kt:11-16`\n- OrderController handles GET and POST for orders: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderController.kt:15-46`\n- OrderRepository is in-memory ConcurrentHashMap: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/order/OrderRepository.kt:10-27`\n- ShipmentRepository stores by shipmentId; has no findByOrderId: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/ShipmentRepository.kt:10-27`\n- Shipment already has a status enum with CREATED, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/shipment/Shipment.kt:23-27`\n- Error handling uses ApiException hierarchy: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiExceptions.kt:11-30`\n- ErrorCode enum needs a new code for order cancellation rejection: `/sample-service/src/main/kotlin/com/unityinflow/sample/api/ApiError.kt:31-37`\n\n**Conventions this repository already has:**\n- All errors are thrown as ApiException subclasses (ConflictException, ResourceNotFoundException); caught by GlobalExceptionHandler\n- Response envelope always wraps errors: `{ \"error\": { \"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\", \"fields\": [...] } }`\n- Controllers return entities directly as JSON; Spring serializes them\n- Status codes: 201 CREATED, 200 OK, 404 NOT_FOUND, 409 CONFLICT\n- Tests use MockMvc with both status and error body assertions\n- In-memory repositories with concurrent stores; no update methods needed, only save/find/exists\n\n**Affected files:**\n1. `Order.kt` — Add status field (ACTIVE | CANCELLED) to entity, because the ticket requires reporting status in GET /orders/{orderId}\n2. `OrderRepository.kt` — No changes needed; save() already handles updates via ConcurrentHashMap\n3. `ShipmentRepository.kt` — Add findByOrderId(orderId: String) method, because cancel must find all shipments of an order\n4. `OrderController.kt` — Add POST /{orderId}/cancel endpoint, because this is the main requirement\n5. `ApiError.kt` — Add ORDER_CANCELLED error code, because creating a shipment for a cancelled order must reject with a distinct error\n6. `OrderControllerTest.kt` — Add tests for cancel endpoint (happy path, already cancelled, has confirmed shipment, unknown order)\n7. `ShipmentControllerTest.kt` — Add test that POST /shipments fails for cancelled orders\n\n**Risks:**\n- Adding status to Order changes JSON schema; existing tests that parse Order fields must not break\n- The all-or-nothing semantics (reject whole cancel if any shipment is CONFIRMED) is race-prone in multithreaded code; in-memory store provides no transaction, so I must check all shipments before mutating any\n- Backwards compatibility: GET /orders and POST /orders must still work; orders created before this change should default to ACTIVE or be backfilled\n\n**Open questions:**\n- Should newly created orders default to ACTIVE status? (Yes; the requirement says \"A newly created order is ACTIVE\".)\n- If a cancel fails due to CONFIRMED shipments, do I need a specific error code beyond 409? (The ticket says \"rejected with HTTP 409\" without naming a code; I will add ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL to follow the pattern of ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS.)\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt**: Add a status field with type OrderStatus (enum with ACTIVE, CANCELLED); update the primary Order constructor and data class to include it.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt**: Add a public method `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to find all shipments matching an orderId. Wait, that's wrong — the repository finds Orders, not Shipments. Instead, I'll add this to ShipmentRepository.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt**: Add `fun findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to filter the store for shipments matching the order.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt**: Add a POST /{orderId}/cancel endpoint that:\n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if order does not exist\n   - Returns 200 with the updated order if it is already CANCELLED (idempotent)\n   - Checks all shipments of the order; if any is CONFIRMED, throws ConflictException and changes nothing\n   - Otherwise, sets order status to CANCELLED, cancels all CREATED shipments, saves, and returns the updated order\n\n5. **ApiError.kt**: Add ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL error code to the ErrorCode enum.\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt**: Add tests:\n   - Cancel an active order, verify 200 and order status is CANCELLED\n   - Cancel an already-cancelled order, verify 200 (idempotent)\n   - Cancel an order with a CONFIRMED shipment, verify 409 and order status unchanged\n   - Cancel a non-existent order, verify 404\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add test:\n   - Create an order, cancel it, POST a new shipment, verify 409 with new error code\n\n**Alternatives considered and rejected:**\n\n- *Use a dedicated CancelOrderRequest/response DTO*: Rejected because the ticket says \"returns the order\", which means the existing Order DTO is sufficient.\n- *Store cancel history (e.g., cancelledAt timestamp)*: Rejected because the ticket only asks for status, not timestamp.\n- *Use a service layer to encapsulate cancel logic*: Rejected because other endpoints (create order, get order) do not use a service layer; this repository uses inline logic in the controller.\n- *Add cancel to ShipmentRepository*: Rejected; cancel is order-scoped logic, belongs in OrderController.\n- *Use a new exception type CancelFailedException*: Rejected because ConflictException already maps to 409 and is used for ORDER_ALREADY_EXISTS; reuse it for ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Caller sends | Service reads | Service writes | Caller receives | Mechanism |\n|------|--------------|----------------|-----------------|-----------------|-----------|\n| Cancel active order | POST /orders/O-1/cancel, no body | Order O-1 (not found) | — | 404 NOT_FOUND, error envelope with ORDER_NOT_FOUND | ResourceNotFoundException |\n| Cancel active order (happy) | POST /orders/O-1/cancel, no body | Order O-1 (ACTIVE), Shipments of O-1 (all CREATED or CANCELLED) | Order O-1 (now CANCELLED), Shipments (CREATED→CANCELLED) | 200 OK, Order with status=CANCELLED | ConcurrentHashMap.put + ShipmentRepository.save in a loop |\n| Cancel already-cancelled order | POST /orders/O-1/cancel, no body | Order O-1 (CANCELLED), Shipments of O-1 (any status) | — | 200 OK, Order with status=CANCELLED (unchanged) | Read-only check, return existing order |\n| Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment | POST /orders/O-1/cancel, no body | Order O-1 (ACTIVE), Shipments of O-1 (includes CONFIRMED) | — | 409 CONFLICT, error envelope with ORDER_CANNOT_CANCEL | ConflictException, rollback implicit (nothing was written) |\n| Create shipment for cancelled order | POST /shipments, orderId=O-1 | Order O-1 (CANCELLED) | — | 409 CONFLICT, error envelope with ORDER_CANCELLED | ConflictException in ShipmentController.create |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest.cancel_active_order**: Create order O-1 (defaults to ACTIVE), POST /orders/O-1/cancel, assert 200 and status=CANCELLED\n2. **OrderControllerTest.cancel_already_cancelled_order**: Create and cancel order O-1, POST /orders/O-1/cancel again, assert 200 and no change\n3. **OrderControllerTest.cancel_order_with_confirmed_shipment**: Create order O-1, create shipment S-1 for O-1, manually update S-1 to CONFIRMED in repository, POST /orders/O-1/cancel, assert 409 and order status still ACTIVE\n4. **OrderControllerTest.cancel_nonexistent_order**: POST /orders/O-999/cancel, assert 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND\n5. **OrderControllerTest.cancel_also_cancels_created_shipments**: Create order O-1, create two shipments S-1 (CREATED) and S-2 (created then manually set CONFIRMED), POST /orders/O-1/cancel, assert 200 and S-1 status now CANCELLED, S-2 still CONFIRMED\n6. **ShipmentControllerTest.create_shipment_for_cancelled_order**: Create order, cancel it, POST /shipments for that order, assert 409 with ORDER_CANCELLED\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the design. I'll start by reading each file I need to modify, then edit them in order."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":348,"cache_read_input_tokens":20649,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":348},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4eeb0473-f999-484e-af22-bd0a5440f210","uuid":"adc51224-afd2-4fa2-b42f-f8b4c9d8fbf3","timestamp":"2026-09-09T10:12:20.028Z","request_id":"req_011Cesgjc3TKYTSK7hatz4rN"}
